{
  "_about": [
    "Do-not-translate terms: what must reach every language exactly as it is in English.",
    "The full list behind 'What not to translate' in docs/translations.md, which gives the kinds of term (2026-10-10): a new term goes here only, a new kind of term there as well.",
    "A term is checked only where the English contains it, and the translation must then carry",
    "it at least as many times. kind 'exact' matches the text (whole words where it starts or",
    "ends with a letter); kind 'code' matches a standalone token. context 'strict' is for codes",
    "that are also ordinary words (As, Leo, Can, Me…): those count only beside a slash or",
    "directly before an angle code ('Su/Mo', 'Ju MC'), never in a sentence. 'pattern' replaces",
    "the literal term with a regular expression.",
    "locales: a language's own established spelling of the term, where its astrologers write one (the house-system eponyms in Cyrillic for Russian, Porfirio in Spanish; 2026-10-09). There the translation carries that spelling instead, matched as a stem so a language that declines names may."
  ],
